{"author": {"email": "team-4@zeonhackathon.app", "user_id": "515bf590-a091-70c1-ad7c-b76beac70085"}, "message": "add arm_and_shelf workflow: interleave arm motion with OpenShelf network calls\n\nAnswers 'how do I actuate the shelf mid-workflow': the shelf skills are ordinary skill\nnodes, so they drop straight into the graph between arm nodes. No special mechanism.\n\n  1 shelf_present   openshelf_retrieve   network: POST + poll until settled\n  2 arm_pick        take_from_shelf      arm\n  3 arm_place       place_on_stand       arm\n  4 shelf_actuate   openshelf_command    network: any path/method/body\n  5 shelf_settle    openshelf_status     network: confirm settled\n\nThe interlock is the edge type, not extra code. openshelf_retrieve returns success\nFalse on settle timeout, so the on_success edge into arm_pick IS the gate - an arm\ncannot enter until the shelf has reported itself settled. That matters because Zeon\nmodels the shelf as a static mesh and the planner cannot see it moving.", "parents": ["611fd92b274cf9337718ecae395262c7a2154c1e57625686b80899431858ebfc"], "tree": "ec1d48611a586e3b60dd396b40c203496494a997324e0e91d82eb07069c731af", "ts": "2026-07-26T19:16:43Z"}